  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Partnerschip Mensen met een Missie - The Peace Project (2024-2031)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity is one of the Strategic Partners of the grant Contributing 
to Peaceful and Safe Societies 2024-2031.

This programme aims to strengthen and support religious actors and other proximate peacebuilders in South Sudan, DR Congo, Burundi and Uganda in transforming harmful convictions and &#x2018;othering&#x2019; into social trust. 

This initiative aims to:

- Bridge intergroup divides, foster cohesion and influence conflict-sensitive and inclusive policies at local, national and international levels;
- Utilize the normative influence, mobilising power, and the extensive network of local (religious) leaders in promoting peace;
- Support and equip individuals with a mission as catalysts for inspiring and initiating transformative change;
- Link local realities with each other, and broader national, regional, and international policies and practices;
- Embrace flexibility, continuous reflection, learning and adaptation;
- Invest in trauma healing as a fundamental pre-requisite for peace.</narrative>
  </description>
